# Explicit identity context consumed by finite import

M06a1 adopts the complete F45 API and all 18 original tests from PR #31, head `7200b3c7583e6c3bd7a474030344323e3fcb93e2`. It preserves eager fresh-v4 consumption, deterministic library-v5 branches over explicit immutable observations, UUID spelling and separate resource/semantic reservation sets. The supplied counter is a deterministic test provider, not an entropy source or graph/library fact adapter.

The actual F14 caller generates distinct identity roles, stages and commits a linked package/part model, then checks all supplied node IDs, the fixed semantic typing target, JSON reopen and undo/redo. Exhausted supplies and cancellation preserve the empty document and existing redo. Its registry is caller-private planning: these checks do not establish transactional allocator rollback or a global reservation service.

`identity_context_probe` measures combined generation, string/role parsing and registry restoration for 256/1024/4096 pairs. Each repetition starts a fresh provider and registry; expected fixtures and full-result checks are outside the timer. Two warmups precede seven retained raw nanosecond samples and min/median/max. This measures one API workload; it supplies no p95, RSS, native/UI speed or application capacity claim and uses no hard timing cutoff.

Run `cargo test --offline --locked --manifest-path rust/crates/syson-domain/Cargo.toml`, the corresponding `syson-text-import` suite, and `cargo run --offline --locked --release --manifest-path rust/crates/syson-domain/Cargo.toml --example identity_context_probe`. Current-source execution remains pending root qualification.

All 38 original donor files remain verbatim archived, including the 166-line SnapshotStore integration and failed lock attempt. That file-backed caller remains mandatory behind its missing workflow/storage prerequisites; JSON reopen does not replace it. M06/M104 graph/library bindings, C01/C02 native comparison, default UI and database/restart acceptance remain open. No original hold is released.
